														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3836122">
									

<p>I thought for some days about the question of making it accessible to the reader, and I have two suggestions that could work for you, either for this, or future articles.</p>
<p>First, you could make two or three versions of the article with distinct clearance levels, so the low level version is the main article, while the high level is the explanation. This model was used on a bunch of good skips. SCP-2317 comes to mind, though it isn't the best example for this article.</p>
<p>Second, you could rely on giving spoilers on the comments. It is a cheap trick for this, but sometimes it is worth it. Though some readers won't even look here, several others are already used to look into the comments to see if they find something about the skip they couldn't see by themselves.</p>
<p>Anyway, my personal opinion stands the same, but it isn't at all a bad execution, and I don't think you have to rewrite this unless you want to. I look forward to read new articles from you.</p>

							</div>

								
					
